      en: "Natal is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Brazil. A sunny city in the northeast, known for its massive sand dunes and fresh sea breeze. Means 'Christmas' in Portuguese. Has the world's largest cashew tree nearby. Famous for buggy rides on the Genipabu dunes. This city is among the characteristic settlements of Brazil, set between the metropolises of São Paulo and Rio de Janeiro and the vast spaces of the interior. Like many notable places in Brazil, it combines regional character with the wider significance of the world's fifth-largest country. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Brazil, where tropical nature, Portuguese heritage, samba, football, and Carnival come together."
