      en: "Petrópolis is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Brazil. The historic summer residence of the Brazilian emperors in the mountains of Rio de Janeiro. Houses the Imperial Museum (Museu Imperial). Was founded by Emperor Dom Pedro II. Popular for its pleasant mountain climate. This city is among the characteristic settlements of Brazil, set between the metropolises of São Paulo and Rio de Janeiro and the vast spaces of the interior. Like many notable places in Brazil, it combines regional character with the wider significance of the world's fifth-largest country. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Brazil, where tropical nature, Portuguese heritage, samba, football, and Carnival come together.",
